From: Gaetan Lepage <gaetan@glepage.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hydra-builder: make the drv available to the pre-build-hook

Nix invokes `pre-build-hook` with the unresolved derivation path, but the
builder only imports the closure of the resolved derivation's inputs, so that
path is not a valid store path on the agent. Hooks that inspect the derivation
-- `nix-required-mounts` reads `requiredSystemFeatures` with
`nix derivation show` to decide which devices to bind into the build sandbox --
therefore cannot see what the step requested, and bind nothing: CUDA steps run
without a GPU.

Ask the queue runner for the derivation alongside the inputs, so it is imported
with them. This is the `hydra-builder` counterpart of the `copyClosureTo` fix
the C++ queue runner needed for the same reason.

Cf. https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/9272.
---
--- a/subprojects/hydra-builder/src/state.rs
+++ b/subprojects/hydra-builder/src/state.rs
@@ -532,10 +532,22 @@
                 JobFailure::Import(eyre::eyre!("failed to decode resolved derivation: {e}"))
             })?;
 
-        // Fetch the transitive closure of the resolved inputs.
+        // Fetch the transitive closure of the resolved inputs, plus the
+        // derivation itself. Nix hands `pre-build-hook` the unresolved drv
+        // path, and hooks that inspect it -- `nix-required-mounts` reads
+        // `requiredSystemFeatures` with `nix derivation show` to decide which
+        // devices to bind into the sandbox -- need it to be a valid store
+        // path. Without it the hook cannot tell what the step asked for and
+        // silently mounts nothing.
+        // Cf. https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/9272.
         let requisites = client
             .fetch_requisites(hydra_proto::StorePaths {
-                paths: basic_drv.inputs.iter().map(ProtoStorePath::from).collect(),
+                paths: basic_drv
+                    .inputs
+                    .iter()
+                    .chain(std::iter::once(&drv))
+                    .map(ProtoStorePath::from)
+                    .collect(),
             })
             .await
             .map_err(|e| JobFailure::Import(e.into()))?
